cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use DriveBench, cite this software and record the exact Git commit and benchmark protocol used."
type: software
title: "DriveBench: Kernel-Tuning Benchmark and RL Environment"
authors:
  - family-names: Mahadik
    given-names: Rahul
repository-code: "https://github.com/rahul-mahadik/driving-world-model-inference"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  DriveBench measures video-model inference and GPU operators, and exposes
  budgeted configuration search through agent tools and a Gymnasium environment.
  Its operator dataset includes CUDA timings, allocated-memory measurements,
  numerical checks and recorded search trajectories. Measured-table replay
  supports CPU policy evaluation; a separate runner confirms fixed selections
  with fresh GPU measurements.
